9. In construing this article, reference was made by both parties in the course of their arguments to the other articles in the same part, namely, articles 324,325,326,327 and 328. Article 324
provides for the constitution and appointment of an Election Commissioner to superintend, direct and control elections to the legislatures;
article 325
prohibits discrimination against electors on the ground of religion, race, caste, or sex;
article 326
provides for adult suffrage;
article 327
empowers Parliament to pass laws making provision with respect to all matters relating to, or in connection with, elections to the legislatures, subject to the provisions of the Constitution; and
article 328
is a complementary article giving power to the State Legislature to make provision with respect to all matters relating to, or in connection with, elections to the State Legislature.
